  "cause": "The authored pool is one1923-byte character array. Native generic text discovery excludes starts under owned spans, and bounded source-pointer resolution only considered declared owners. Correct148 typed pointer targets therefore rendered as parent-plus-offset and character rows. The byte pool declaration was too coarse for entity-level output, and the framework did not expose subordinate records.",
  "implementation": [
    "Use already resolved typed source-pointer fields and explicit character-owner extents; never scan arbitrary LONGs for plausible text addresses. Validate NUL bounds, supported bytes and final code/data ownership.",
    "Create inferred string records beneath the unchanged parent. A suffix pointer binds to its containing record plus the real addend; it does not invent a new string start.",
    "Inferred names combine sanitized literal content and source section/offset, with deterministic collision handling. Authored names win, duplicate text at distinct addresses stays distinct, and shared pointers reuse one label.",
    "Feed inferred records into the existing range/owner resolver and frozen rendering path. Inferred names remain generated, not authored declarations. No manual generated-source edits or game-specific constants.",
    "Within an established character pool, render supported unreferenced NUL records without labels/consumers. Controls, quotes, backslashes, unsupported bytes and boundaries preserve original storage.",
    "Snapshot the policy input count and copy retained owner/ref values across append operations, because the authoritative IR also grows a policy mirror. A growth fixture exercises22 policy items rather than assuming an allocation bucket."
  ],
